WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.339 --> 00:00:04.640
Fans are yelling, crying, and cheering as
the credits roll on Avengers: Endgame.

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:08.320
But there's another emotion viewers are experiencing:
confusion.

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:10.830
Major spoilers ahead, so consider yourself
warned!

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:11.830
The kid at Stark's funeral

00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:16.119
At the end of Avengers: Endgame, nearly all
the MCU heroes gather to pay tribute to Tony

00:00:16.119 --> 00:00:17.789
Stark's life and death.

00:00:17.789 --> 00:00:20.880
During the funeral, we see a familiar-looking
boy in a suit.

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:23.860
It's actually a blink-and-you'll-miss-it cameo.

00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:28.240
Played by Ty Simpkins, the character is actually
Harley Keener, the gadget-loving kid who helped

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:30.820
Tony out of a jam in Iron Man 3.

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:31.880
"Freeze!

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:35.560
Don't move."

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:37.160
"You got me."

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:41.000
The Russo Brothers were determined to answer
almost every lingering question in the film

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:45.570
franchise, and this cameo also offers a hint
about what we can expect from the MCU in the

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:46.570
future.

00:00:46.570 --> 00:00:51.420
While Morgan Stark, Pepper Potts, and Rhodey
are all candidates for future Iron Man films,

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:54.700
Harley is one of the youngest heroes of the
Marvel universe.

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:59.880
Endgame is the culmination of over a decade
of storytelling and multiple actors' contracts.

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:04.389
Like Tom Holland's Spider-Man and Brie Larson's
Captain Marvel, the future stars of the MCU

00:01:04.389 --> 00:01:07.200
are going to be a younger generation of performers.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.899
Harley could quite conceivably be a future
Iron Kid.

00:01:09.899 --> 00:01:10.899
Sam and the shield

00:01:10.899 --> 00:01:14.770
It sounds like Chris Evans has been ready
to move on from the MCU for years, but at

00:01:14.770 --> 00:01:18.009
least he gets to leave the franchise on his
own terms.

00:01:18.009 --> 00:01:22.560
After going back in time to return the Infinity
Stones to their proper places and times, Captain

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:26.479
America decides to stick around and marry
Peggy Carter, living out his life until the

00:01:26.479 --> 00:01:30.179
year 2023, where we see him as an old man.

00:01:30.179 --> 00:01:35.069
But just because Chris Evans is done with
the MCU doesn't mean Captain America is.

00:01:35.069 --> 00:01:37.670
Steve presents Sam Wilson with the iconic
shield.

00:01:37.670 --> 00:01:39.509
Meanwhile, Bucky looks on approvingly.

00:01:39.509 --> 00:01:44.740
Still, a big question remains: Why was Sam
given the shield and not Bucky, especially

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:48.109
since both of them have worn the mantle of
Captain America in the comics?

00:01:48.109 --> 00:01:50.029
Well, there are a few reasons.

00:01:50.029 --> 00:01:53.969
For one, Bucky really seems to like his life
in Wakanda, and he's already got his own new

00:01:53.969 --> 00:01:56.590
superhero identity: the White Wolf.

00:01:56.590 --> 00:01:58.420
"Good morning Sergeant Barnes."

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.240
"Bucky."

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:04.280
"How are you feeling?"

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:05.520
"Good."

00:02:05.849 --> 00:02:10.680
Another reason: Captain America never actually
chose Bucky as his successor in the comics.

00:02:10.689 --> 00:02:14.830
Instead, Bucky took over for Cap after Steve
Rogers died.

00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:18.959
Cap was proud of his one-time sidekick, but
the only person he's ever actively passed

00:02:18.959 --> 00:02:20.980
the shield onto was Sam Wilson.

00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:25.379
Really, it's only fitting that Cap would pass
his shield along in the same fashion in Avengers:

00:02:25.379 --> 00:02:26.379
Endgame.

00:02:26.379 --> 00:02:27.379
Captain Thormerica

00:02:27.379 --> 00:02:30.530
It's one of the best moments in Avengers:
Endgame: Thanos is just about to kill Thor

00:02:30.530 --> 00:02:34.780
when he's smacked in the back of the head
by Captain America, who now wields the mighty

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:36.340
hammer Mjolnir.

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:40.489
But you might be wondering how Steve Rogers
was finally able to lift the hammer, especially

00:02:40.489 --> 00:02:43.550
when he couldn't quite pull it off in Avengers:
Age of Ultron.

00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:46.180
A few different theories are floating around.

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:51.329
Some speculate that Cap could fully lift Mjolnir
in Age of Ultron but simply chose not to.

00:02:51.329 --> 00:02:54.099
"That's a very, very interesting theory.

00:02:54.099 --> 00:02:58.950
I have a simpler one: You're all not worthy."

00:02:58.950 --> 00:02:59.950
"Boo!"

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:01.140
"Aw, c'mon."

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:04.879
At the time, Cap was still struggling with
his ego and trying to find his place in the

00:03:04.879 --> 00:03:10.200
world, but the Captain America we see in Endgame
is a changed man: He's let go of his ego and

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:12.739
admits Tony was right to be worried about
Thanos.

00:03:12.739 --> 00:03:15.660
He wants to make amends with his old friend.

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:19.920
Just like Thor, Steve needed to get over himself
to become the hero he was always destined

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:20.920
to be.

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:21.920
Did Cap ruin the timeline?

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:25.040
While trying to grab a couple of Infinity
Stones, Iron Man and Ant-Man accidently let

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:27.150
Loki get away with the Tesseract.

00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:32.430
This complicates things when Cap from 2012
runs into Cap from 2023, who happens to be

00:03:32.430 --> 00:03:34.139
carrying the scepter.

00:03:34.139 --> 00:03:38.650
Past Cap obviously thinks Present Cap is Loki
in disguise, and their ensuing battle is a

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:40.750
true highlight of the film.

00:03:40.750 --> 00:03:45.400
Present Cap gets the upper hand by telling
Past Cap that Bucky is actually alive; a wrinkle

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:48.189
that seems to complicate the future timeline.

00:03:48.189 --> 00:03:53.129
The fight ends when Present Cap zaps Past
Cap with the scepter, but what about the aftermath?

00:03:53.129 --> 00:03:57.880
Fortunately, the scepter also has mind control
powers, thanks to the Mind Stone… not to

00:03:57.880 --> 00:03:59.999
mention that Loki is on the loose.

00:03:59.999 --> 00:04:03.770
Not only would it be easy to assume that Past
Cap's memories were messed up by the Mind

00:04:03.770 --> 00:04:08.249
Stone, but the Avengers would probably assume
everything was Loki's work, from the fight

00:04:08.249 --> 00:04:10.049
to the information about Bucky.

00:04:10.049 --> 00:04:13.700
That means the timeline is still secure, so
rest easy tonight.

